 "152670327ae0": {
  "gloss": "<someone_Seth_meets>",
  "tier": "A",
  "n": 4,
  "evidence": "K&T's entry for the epithet family gives '152520327ae0 006v (4x) <someone Seth meets>'. This sign is that spelling with one glyph changed and it stands four times on 006v and nowhere else, which is their count and their folio exactly. The gloss is their category, not an English word: they did not identify the figure either"
 },
 "680ae0877": {
  "gloss": "be_saved",
  "tier": "A",
  "n": 3,
  "evidence": "K&T's exist entry (670ae0) lists 680ae0 among its variant spellings, citing 072v06, 138v07, 139v06, 140r05, 182v04, 05 and 188r09; 520ae0877 and 670ae0877 are already read as 'be saved'. All three occurrences take it: 072v:7 is Mark 16:16 'he that believeth and is baptized shall be saved', 152r:2 sets it against 'damned', 182v:5 repeats the formula"
 },
 "521774": {
  "gloss": "at_table",
  "tier": "A",
  "n": 3,
  "evidence": "K&T's table entry cites their 774 at 072r08, 072r11, 088v12 and 191r04. This sign stands at 072r:8, 072r:11 and 191r:4 -- three of those four lines -- and carries their 774 under a preposition. It is Mark 16:14, 'afterward he appeared unto the eleven as they sat at meat, and upbraided them with their unbelief': the codex has 'the apostles sat at table in Jerusalem, in the Lord's house' and then 'began to admonish them on believing'"
 },
 "5204149623f2": {
  "gloss": "hateth",
  "tier": "B",
  "n": 4,
  "evidence": "1 John 4:20, named in the translation of 099r-099v: 'he that loveth not his brother whom he hath seen, how can he love God whom he hath not seen'. All four occurrences stand in that passage: 099v:4 reads 'brother [hateth], loves somebody how? this somebody God loves' almost word for word, 099r:10 and 099v:2 'brother [hateth] ... love'. hate is a word no sign carried (ktcross) and it is the one content word of the passage the pool tool (ktleft.py) left free that fits every line. One passage, so not A."
 },
 "5202b7": {
  "gloss": "became",
  "tier": "C",
  "n": 2,
  "evidence": "Genesis 2:7, 'and man became a living soul'. Both occurrences stand immediately before the codex's 'to-soul-one': 002v:10 'and [became] a living soul', 122r:3 '[became] a living soul, breathed on Adam'. become is carried by K&T's b30, but the passage pool (ktleft.py, Genesis 2:7 widened one verse) offered became as free and it is the only word of the verse that fits the slot both times."
 },
 "70d520": {
  "gloss": "dust",
  "tier": "C",
  "n": 3,
  "evidence": "Genesis 2:7, 'the Lord God formed man of the dust of the ground'. 002v:9 'Paradise, the Lord God, Adam ... [dust] and then', 002v:10 'Adam was ... the aforesaid [dust] and became a soul', 122r:1 'out of Paradise the Lord God, Adam ... [dust]'. The passage pool (ktleft.py) left became, dust, eastward, mist, nostrils and planted free; dust is the one that reads with 'the aforesaid' on 002v:10. Not nostrils: breath is taken and nothing in the three lines is 'into'."
 },
 "ab0": {
  "gloss": "gate/open",
  "tier": "B",
  "n": 3,
  "evidence": "K&T's four spellings of gate and open all end in this sign: 0600a2ab0 'gate, open (up)', 060520ab0 'gate', 0a2060ab0 'gate'. Alone it stands at 006r:4 '[gate] Garden of Eden, and then Seth appeared (before) God' -- the Vita Adae has Seth at the gates of Paradise; 101r:5 'Elijah raptured to heaven most high and [opened]'; 216r:2 '[opened] heaven ... and Stephen saw' (Acts 7:56 'I see the heavens opened'). Three passages, all fit. The gloss is K&T's for the longer spellings; what the affixes 060, 0a2 and 520 add is not read."
 },
 "ab0ab0": {
  "gloss": "gates",
  "tier": "C",
  "n": 2,
  "evidence": "Reduplication of ab0 (gate/open), the pattern K&T read as woman from 060131. Both occurrences are the same sentence in the doubled Life of Adam: 007r:2 and 125r:3 '[gates] was Adam (on) the earth to till the ground' -- Genesis 3:23-24, sent out of the garden. One sentence twice, so C."
 },
 "432670": {
  "gloss": "chapter",
  "tier": "B",
  "n": 2,
  "evidence": "K&T's chapter is 670; this is 432 + 670 and stands after a numeral both times: 088v:3 'six [chapter] written', 092v:7 '14 [chapter] in'. The codex's chapter citations elsewhere are 'holy Matthew, in the Nth chapter'. Read as chapter under whatever 432 marks (an ordinal or case ending); 432 itself is not read."
 },
 "845152222": {
  "gloss": "exceed",
  "tier": "C",
  "n": 3,
  "evidence": "Matthew 5:20, 'except your righteousness shall exceed the righteousness of the scribes and Pharisees, ye shall in no case enter into the kingdom of heaven'. 109r:7 'he who the scribes [exceed]', 109v:1 'somebody does not ... he who the scribes [exceed]', 109r:6 '[exceed] and from somebody is this righteous'. The passage pool (ktleft.py) left exceed and enter free; enter does not stand next to 'the scribes'. One passage."
 },
 "520af0": {
  "gloss": "garment",
  "tier": "C",
  "n": 2,
  "evidence": "John 13:12, 'after he had washed their feet, and had taken his garments, and was set down again'. 030r:11 'washed the feet, [garment] [?] and', 030r:10 '[garment] [?] and the two ... apostles in the middle'. garment and raiment are free (ktcross); clothes is taken by 520b7a and its family. The second hole on both lines is not read. One passage."
 },
 "5202d6": {
  "gloss": "enter",
